      "summaries": {
        "en": "whatsapp-web.js is a Node.js library that enables programmatic interaction with WhatsApp by connecting through the WhatsApp Web interface, solving the need for automated messaging and bot functionality without official APIs. It works by simulating a real browser session using Puppeteer, maintaining persistent connections to handle messages, media, and group chats. Developers can use it to build chatbots for customer support, automate notifications, or create custom WhatsApp tools by extending its event-driven architecture with JavaScript.",
        "zh": "whatsapp-web.js 是一个基于 Node.js 的库，通过连接 WhatsApp Web 界面实现程序化交互，解决了在没有官方 API 的情况下构建自动化消息和聊天机器人的需求。其核心机制是利用 Puppeteer 模拟真实浏览器会话，维持持久连接以处理消息、媒体和群聊功能。开发者可用它创建客户服务聊天机器人、自动化通知系统或定制化工具，通过扩展其事件驱动架构，结合 JavaScript 生态快速实现各种实际应用场景。",
        "es": "whatsapp-web.js is a Node.js library that enables programmatic interaction with WhatsApp by connecting through the WhatsApp Web interface, solving the need for automated messaging and bot functionality without official APIs. It works by simulating a real browser session using Puppeteer, maintaining persistent connections to handle messages, media, and group chats. Developers can use it to build chatbots for customer support, automate notifications, or create custom WhatsApp tools by extending its event-driven architecture with JavaScript.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "whatsapp-web.js stands out for api, bot, and bot-api in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "whatsapp-web.js is a Node.js library that enables programmatic interaction with WhatsApp by connecting through the WhatsApp Web interface, solving the need for automated messaging and bot functionality without official APIs. It works by simulating a real browser session using Puppeteer, maintaining persistent connections to handle messages, media, and group chats. Developers can use it to build chatbots for customer support, automate notifications, or create custom WhatsApp tools by extending its event-driven architecture with JavaScript.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/pedroslopez/whatsapp-web.js for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
      },
